  "answer": "The goal was not met. Repeats confirmed three settings, each on a different scene, and the policy is clearly at fault in only two of them. Every repeat failed at 096988dd with the car at 1.25x and the ego at 1.2x (S4), and at 19f339ba with the car at 2x and the ego at 1.2x (S41). In both, the policy steered into a car in the next lane: at 096988dd it drifted left against a RIGHT command, and at 19f339ba it braked hard on an open road for no clear reason. The third setting, 1c45ce3a with the car at 1.25x and the ego at 0.8x (S44), also failed every repeat. But in most of those runs a replayed car that does not react cut into the ego from the right, so this case says more about replayed traffic than about the policy. All three rest on a handful of repeats, so their ranges only just clear 0.5. In none of them did the ego hit the retimed car itself. What seems to matter is the ego's speed at hand-off, which moves the ego relative to the replayed traffic beside it. No failure was flagged as a possible simulator artifact.",
